INSERT INTO `ci_abx_texts` VALUES
(1,'>=90','0','LOW BV RISK - The presence of protective Lactobacilli in the absence of typical BV organisms may indicate a healthy vaginal microbiome. In some cases, such as following antibiotic treatment, it could also represent a Lactobacilli overgrowth.','Typical bacterial vaginosis organisms were not detected. If Cytolytic Vaginosis is a concern (Lactobacillus overgrowth, low vaginal pH), sitz baths with baking soda could be considered.','bv'),
(3,'>=90','1','LOW BV RISK - The presence of protective Lactobacilli, even alongside typically pathogenic organisms, may indicate a healthy vaginal microbiome. BV is characterized by a decrease in beneficial Lactobacilli and an overgrowth of other bacteria.','Treatment for Bacterial Vaginosis may not be necessary unless symptoms or other clinical factors suggest otherwise.','bv'),
(4,'70-90','1','LOW-INTERMEDIATE BV RISK - Protective Lactobacilli along with typically BV related bacteria may indicate a sligtly disrupted vagianal microbiome. BV is characterized by a decrease in beneficial Lactobacilli and an overgrowth of other bacteria.','Treatment for BV could be considered, particularly if risk factors such as pregnancy, surgery, or recurrent infections are present.','bv'),
(5,'30-70','1','INTERMEDIATE BV RISK - While protective Lactobacilli are present, the detection of BV related bacteria may indicate a disrupted vaginal microbiome. BV is characterized by a decrease in beneficial Lactobacilli and an overgrowth of other bacteria.','Treatment for BV may be warranted, particularly if clinical symptoms confirm infection or if risk factors such as pregnancy, surgery, or recurrent infections are present.','bv'),
(6,'<30','1','HIGH BV RISK - The presence of BV related bacteria may indicate a disrupted vaginal microbiome. BV is characterized by a decrease in beneficial Lactobacilli and an overgrowth of other bacteria.','Treatment for BV may be warranted, particularly if clinical symptoms confirm infection or if risk factors such as pregnancy, surgery, or recurrent infections are present.','bv'),
(7,'none','1','HIGH BV RISK - The presence of BV related bacteria and a lack of Lactobacilli may indicate a disrupted vaginal microbiome. BV is characterized by a decrease in beneficial Lactobacilli and an overgrowth of other bacteria.','Treatment for BV may be warranted, particularly if clinical symptoms confirm infection or if risk factors such as pregnancy, surgery, or recurrent infections are present.','bv'),
(8,'none','0','INDERTEMINATE RESULTS - Both protective Lactobacilli and BV bacteria are absent. Additional clinical and laboratory data may be needed to establish a diagnosis.','Typical bacterial vaginosis organisms are not present. BV treatment may not be warranted unless symptoms or other clinical factors suggest otherwise.','bv');
