(3,'Citrobacter koseri','Aerobic gram-negative bacilli. A normal part of the environment and gut flora. Usually, a nosocomial pathogen in compromised hosts, elderly, and neonates.\nPlasmid-carried genes can confer resistance to beta-lactams, fluoroquinolones, TMP-SMX, and aminoglycosides.\nNitrofurantoin is variable in activity.\nPlease note: Additional resistance mechanisms may confer Fluoroquinolone resistance without the regular Qnr markers.\n','Fosfomycin.\nTMP-SMX. \nNitrofurantoin.\nCefepime.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin.\nMeropenem, Imipenem-Cilastatin.\nCeftazidime-Avibactam.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nCeftolozane-Tazobactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.\nCefiderocol.',0,'NULL','','Fosfomycin.\nTMP-SMX. \nNitrofurantoin.\nCefepime.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin.\nMeropenem, Imipenem-Cilastatin.\nCeftazidime-Avibactam.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nCeftolozane-Tazobactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.\nCefiderocol.','Fosfomycin.\nTMP-SMX. \nNitrofurantoin.\nCefepime.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin.\nMeropenem, Imipenem-Cilastatin.\nCeftazidime-Avibactam.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nCeftolozane-Tazobactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.\nCefiderocol.','Fosfomycin.\nTMP-SMX. \nNitrofurantoin.\nCefepime.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin.\nMeropenem, Imipenem-Cilastatin.\nCeftazidime-Avibactam.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.\nCefiderocol.','Fosfomycin.\nTMP-SMX. \nNitrofurantoin.\nCefepime.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin.\nMeropenem, Imipenem-Cilastatin.\nCeftazidime-Avibactam.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.\nCefiderocol.','Fosfomycin.\nTMP-SMX. \nNitrofurantoin.\nCefepime.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin.\nMeropenem, Imipenem-Cilastatin.\nCeftazidime-Avibactam.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nImipenem-Cilas