(4,'Citrobacter','Aerobic gram-negative bacilli. A normal part of the environment and gut flora. Usually, a nosocomial pathogen in compromised hosts, elderly, and neonates.\nC. freundii encodes inducible ampC genes; antibiotic selection should consider this whenever C. freundii is detected, regardless of the in vitro susceptibility results.\nPlasmid-carried genes can confer resistance to beta-lactams, fluoroquinolones, TMP-SMX, and aminoglycosides.\nNitrofurantoin is variable in activity.\nPlease note: Additional resistance mechanisms may confer Fluoroquinolone resistance without the regular Qnr markers.\n','Fosfomycin.\nTMP-SMX. \nNitrofurantoin.\nCefepime.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin.\nMeropenem, Imipenem-Cilastatin.\nCeftazidime-Avibactam.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nCeftolozane-Tazobactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.\nCefiderocol.\n',0,'NULL','','Fosfomycin.\nTMP-SMX. \nNitrofurantoin.\nCefepime.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin.\nMeropenem, Imipenem-Cilastatin.\nCeftazidime-Avibactam.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nCeftolozane-Tazobactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.\nCefiderocol.\n','Fosfomycin.\nTMP-SMX. \nNitrofurantoin.\nCefepime.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin.\nMeropenem, Imipenem-Cilastatin.\nCeftazidime-Avibactam.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nCeftolozane-Tazobactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.\nCefiderocol.\n','Fosfomycin.\nTMP-SMX. \nNitrofurantoin.\nCefepime.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin.\nMeropenem, Imipenem-Cilastatin.\nCeftazidime-Avibactam.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.\nCefiderocol.\n','Fosfomycin.\nTMP-SMX. \nNitrofurantoin.\nCefepime.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin.\nMeropenem, Imipenem-Cilastatin.\nCeftazidime-Avibactam.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.\nCefiderocol.\n','Fosfomycin.\nTMP-SMX. \nNitrofurantoin.\nC