(5,'Escherichia coli','\nAerobic, gram-negative bacteria.The most common cause of UTIs. Antibiotic-resistant E. Coli is common in complicated and recurrent UTIs.\nCommonly resistant to cephalosporins, beta-lactam inhibitors, and carbapenems.\nPLEASE NOTE: Additional mechanisms of antibiotic resistance (efflux pumps, decreased membrane permeability, etc.) may confer intrinsic ABX resistance even in the absence of the regular markers (negative PCR results).\n\n','Nitrofurantoin.\nTMP-SMX.\nFosfomycin.\nCefixime.\nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nCeftriaxone, Cefepime.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem.\nCeftazidime-Avibactam.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nCeftolozane-Tazobactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.\nCefiderocol.',0,'NULL','','Nitrofurantoin.\nTMP-SMX.\nFosfomycin.\nCefixime.\nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nCeftriaxone, Cefepime.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem.\nCeftazidime-Avibactam.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nCeftolozane-Tazobactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.\nCefiderocol.','Nitrofurantoin.\nTMP-SMX.\nFosfomycin.\nCefixime.\nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nCeftriaxone, Cefepime.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem.\nCeftazidime-Avibactam.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nCeftolozane-Tazobactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.\nCefiderocol.','Nitrofurantoin.\nTMP-SMX.\nFosfomycin.\nCefepime.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem.\nCeftazidime-Avibactam.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.\nCefiderocol.','Nitrofurantoin.\nTMP-SMX.\nFosfomycin.\nCefepime.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem.\nCeftazidime-Avibactam.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.\nCefiderocol.','Nitrofurantoin.\nTMP-SMX.\nFosfomycin.\nCefepime.\nCiprof