(6,'Enterobacter cloacae','Gram-negative, aerobic, motile bacilli. Common in recurrent UTIs, often catheter or instrumentation-related. \nCommonly resistant to cephalosporins, carbapenems, aminoglycosides, and fluoroquinolones. Fosfomycin - moderately susceptible.\nPLEASE NOTE: Additional resistance mechanisms (efflux pumps, decreased membrane permeability) may confer ABX resistance without the regular resistance markers (negative PCR results).\n','TMP-SMX.\nFosfomycin.\nNitrofurantoin.\nCefepime.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem.\nCeftazidime-Avibactam.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nCeftolozane-Tazobactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.\nCefiderocol.\n\n',0,'NULL','','TMP-SMX.\nFosfomycin.\nNitrofurantoin.\nCefepime.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem.\nCeftazidime-Avibactam.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nCeftolozane-Tazobactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.\nCefiderocol.','TMP-SMX.\nFosfomycin.\nNitrofurantoin.\nCefepime.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem.\nCeftazidime-Avibactam.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nCeftolozane-Tazobactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.\nCefiderocol.','TMP-SMX.\nFosfomycin.\nNitrofurantoin.\nCefepime.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem.\nCeftazidime-Avibactam.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.\nCefiderocol.','TMP-SMX.\nFosfomycin.\nNitrofurantoin.\nCefepime.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem.\nCeftazidime-Avibactam.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.\nCefiderocol.','TMP-SMX.\nFosfomycin.\nNitrofurantoin.\nCefepime.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem.\nCeftazidime-Avibactam.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nImipenem-Cilasta