(7,'Enterobacter/Klebsiella','Gram-negative, aerobic, motile bacilli. Can cause complicated and uncomplicated UTIs, often catheter or instrumentation-related.\nGram-negative, aerobic, motile bacilli.\nColonizes intestinal and respiratory tracts. It can cause complicated and uncomplicated UTIs, often catheter or instrumentation-related.\nFosfomycin - moderately susceptible.\nResistance mechanisms: Constitutive beta-lactamases, Plasmid-mediated ESBL, Metallo-beta-lactamases, and OXA carbapenemases.\nPLEASE NOTE: Additional mechanisms of antibiotic resistance (efflux pumps, decreased membrane permeability, etc.) may confer intrinsic ABX resistance in the absence of the regular markers (negative PCR results).','TMP-SMX.\nCefepime.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nNitrofurantoin.\nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem.\nCeftazidime-Avibactam.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nCeftolozane-Tazobactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.\nCefiderocol.',0,'NULL','','TMP-SMX.\nCefepime.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nNitrofurantoin.\nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem.\nCeftazidime-Avibactam.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nCeftolozane-Tazobactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.\nCefiderocol.\n','TMP-SMX.\nCefepime.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nNitrofurantoin.\nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem.\nCeftazidime-Avibactam.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nCeftolozane-Tazobactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.\nCefiderocol.\n','TMP-SMX.\nCefepime.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nNitrofurantoin.\nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem.\nCeftazidime-Avibactam.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.\nCefiderocol.\n','TMP-SMX.\nCefepime.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nNitrofurantoin.\nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem.\nCeftazidime-Avibactam.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.\nCefiderocol.\n','TMP-SMX.\nCef