(11,'Morganella morganii','Facultative anaerobic gram-negative rod. A normal part of colonic flora and ubiquitous in the environment. UTIs are usually catheter or instrumentation-related, often in compromised hosts.\nConstitutive resistance to 1st and 2nd gen. cephalosporins, fosfomycin, and macrolides.\n\nPLEASE NOTE: Additional mechanisms of antibiotic resistance (efflux pumps, decreased membrane permeability, etc.) may confer intrinsic ABX resistance even in the absence of the regular markers (negative PCR results).','TMP-SMX.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nCeftriaxone, Cefepime.\nCefixime.\nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin.\nMeropenem.\nCeftazidime-Avibactam.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nCeftolozane-Tazobactam.\nCefiderocol.\n',0,'NULL','','TMP-SMX.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nCeftriaxone, Cefepime.\nCefixime.\nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin.\nMeropenem.\nCeftazidime-Avibactam.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nCeftolozane-Tazobactam.\nCefiderocol.','TMP-SMX.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nCeftriaxone, Cefepime.\nCefixime.\nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin.\nMeropenem.\nCeftazidime-Avibactam.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nCeftolozane-Tazobactam.\nCefiderocol.','TMP-SMX.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nCefepime.\nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin.\nMeropenem.\nCeftazidime-Avibactam.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nCefiderocol.','TMP-SMX.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nCefepime.\nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin.\nMeropenem.\nCeftazidime-Avibactam.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nCefiderocol.','TMP-SMX.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nCefepime.\nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin.\nMeropenem.\nCeftazidime-Avibactam.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nCefiderocol.','TMP-SMX.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nCefepime.\nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin.\nMeropenem.\nCeftazidime-Avibactam.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nCefiderocol.','TMP-SMX.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nCefepime.\nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin.\nMeropenem.\nCeftazidime-Avibactam.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nCefiderocol.','