(12,'Pantoea agglomerans','Facultative anerobic, Gram-negative rod, formerly Enterobacter agglomerans. Ubiquitous in the enviroment, but a rare cause of human infection. Cases have been reported mostly among pediatric, hospitalized, immunocompromised, or cancer patients.   \nScant susceptibility data but likely similar in susceptibility to other Enterobacter spp. \nPLEASE NOTE: Pathogenicity unclear, may be a contaminant. Treat if symptomatic. If more pathogenic bacteria are present, treatment choices should prioritize them. ','Amoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nFosfomycin.\nTMP-SMX.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nCeftazidime, Cefepime.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem.\nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin. \n\n',0,'NULL','0','Amoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nFosfomycin.\nTMP-SMX.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nCeftazidime, Cefepime.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem.\nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin. \n\n','Amoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nFosfomycin.\nTMP-SMX.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nCeftazidime, Cefepime.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem.\nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin. \n\n','Fosfomycin.\nTMP-SMX.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nCefepime.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem.\nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin. \n\n','Fosfomycin.\nTMP-SMX.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nCefepime.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem.\nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin. \n\n','Fosfomycin.\nTMP-SMX.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nCefepime.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem.\nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin. \n\n','Fosfomycin.\nTMP-SMX.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nCefepime.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem.\nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin. \n\n','Fosfomycin.\nTMP-SMX.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nCefepime.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem.\nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin. \n\n','Fosfomycin.\nTMP-SMX.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nCefepime.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem.\nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin. \n\n','Fosfomycin.\nTMP-SMX.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nCefepime.\nMe