(13,'Proteus mirabilis','Aerobic, Gram-negative, urease-splitting rod. Causes about 10% of uncomplicated UTIs. More common as a cause of recurrent and catheter-related UTIs.\nIntrinsically resistant to Polymyxins (Colistin), Tigecycline, Nitrofurantoin, and Imipenem.\nOther resistance mechanisms: Inducible ampC-type resistance common (antibiotic selection should consider this regardless of the in vitro susceptibility results), Metallo-beta-lactamases production.\nPLEASE NOTE: Additional mechanisms of antibiotic resistance (efflux pumps, decreased membrane permeability, etc.) may confer intrinsic ABX resistance even in the absence of the regular markers (negative PCR results).','Amoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nCefixime.\nTMP-SMX. \nFosfomycin.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin.\nCefepime.\nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin.\nMeropenem.\nCeftazidime-Avibactam.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nCeftolozane-Tazobactam.\nCefiderocol.\n\n',0,'NULL','','Amoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nCefixime.\nTMP-SMX. \nFosfomycin.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin.\nCefepime.\nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin.\nMeropenem.\nCeftazidime-Avibactam.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nCeftolozane-Tazobactam.\nCefiderocol.\n','Amoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nCefixime.\nTMP-SMX. \nFosfomycin.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin.\nCefepime.\nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin.\nMeropenem.\nCeftazidime-Avibactam.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nCeftolozane-Tazobactam.\nCefiderocol.\n','TMP-SMX. \nFosfomycin.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin.\nCefepime.\nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin.\nMeropenem.\nCeftazidime-Avibactam.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nCefiderocol.\n','TMP-SMX. \nFosfomycin.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin.\nCefepime.\nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin.\nMeropenem.\nCeftazidime-Avibactam.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nCefiderocol.\n','TMP-SMX. \nFosfomycin.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin.\nCefepime.\nGentamicin, Tobramycin, Plazomicin.\nMeropenem.\nCeftazidime-Avibactam.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nCefiderocol.\n','TMP-SMX. \nFosfomycin.\nCiprofloxacin, 