(17,'Serratia marcescens','Aerobic, gram-negative rod, Klebsiella tribe. UTIs are often catheter or instrumentation-related.\nIntrinsically resistant to polymyxins (Polymyxin B, Colistin), Ampicillin-sulbactam, Amoxicillin-clavulanate, 1st gen. cephalosporins, macrolides, and nitrofurantoin.\nOther resistance mechanisms: plasmid beta-lactamases, plasmid-mediated ESBLs, and production of class B metallo-beta-lactamases (NDM, VIM, IMP).\nPlease note: Carbapenem resistance is possible without the expression of the regular markers (negative PCR results).\nPlease note: Fluoroquinolone resistance is usually due to chromosomal mutations - resistance is possible without the expression of the regular QNR markers.','TMP-SMX. \nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nCeftazidime, Cefepime.\nMeropenem, Imipenem-Cilastatin.\nPlazomicin, Tobramycin, Gentamicin.\nCeftazidime-Avibactam.\nCeftolozane-Tazobactam.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.\nCefiderocol.\n',0,'NULL','','TMP-SMX. \nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nCeftazidime, Cefepime.\nMeropenem, Imipenem-Cilastatin.\nPlazomicin, Tobramycin, Gentamicin.\nCeftazidime-Avibactam.\nCeftolozane-Tazobactam.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.\nCefiderocol.\n','TMP-SMX. \nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nCeftazidime, Cefepime.\nMeropenem, Imipenem-Cilastatin.\nPlazomicin, Tobramycin, Gentamicin.\nCeftazidime-Avibactam.\nCeftolozane-Tazobactam.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.\nCefiderocol.\n','TMP-SMX. \nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nCefepime.\nMeropenem, Imipenem-Cilastatin.\nPlazomicin, Tobramycin, Gentamicin.\nCeftazidime-Avibactam.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.\nCefiderocol.\n','TMP-SMX. \nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nCefepime.\nMeropenem, Imipenem-Cilastatin.\nPlazomicin, Tobramycin, Gentamicin.\nCeftazidime-Avibactam.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.\nCefiderocol.\n','TMP-SMX. \nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nCefepime.\n