(18,'Actinobaculum schaalii','Facultative anaerobic gram-positive rod. GU tract commensal and an emerging uropathogen, particularly in elderly men and young children.\nSusceptible to beta-lactams and clindamycin.\nPossible resistance to fluoroquinolones, TMP-SMX, and metronidazole.\nPLEASE NOTE: Pathogenicity unclear, may be a contaminant. Treat if symptomatic. If more pathogenic bacteria are present, treatment choices should prioritize them. \n','Penicillin, Ampicillin, Amoxicillin.\nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nFosfomycin.\nVancomycin.\nDoxycycline.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem. \n',1,'NULL','0','Penicillin, Ampicillin, Amoxicillin.\nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nFosfomycin.\nVancomycin.\nDoxycycline.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem. ','Penicillin, Ampicillin, Amoxicillin.\nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nFosfomycin.\nVancomycin.\nDoxycycline.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem. ','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','Penicillin, Ampicillin, Amoxicillin.\nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nFosfomycin.\nVancomycin.\nDoxycycline.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem. ','Penicillin, Ampicillin, Amoxicillin.\nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nFosfomycin.\nVancomycin.\nDoxycycline.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem. ','Penicillin, Ampicillin, Amoxicillin.\nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nFosfomycin.\nVancomycin.\nDoxycycline.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem. ','Penicillin, Ampicillin, Amoxicillin.\nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nFosfomycin.\nVancomycin.\nDoxycycline.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem. ','Penicillin, Ampicillin, Amoxicillin.\nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nFosfomycin.\nVancomycin.\nDoxycycline.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem. ','','','','','','','','','Penicillin, Ampicillin, Amoxicillin.\nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nFosfomycin.\nVancomycin.\nDoxycycline.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem. ','Penicillin, Ampicillin, Amoxicillin.\nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nFosfomycin.\nVancomycin.\nDoxycycline.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem. ','Penicillin, Ampicillin, Amoxicillin.\nAmoxicillin-Clavul