(20,'Aerococcus urinae','Facultative gram-positive coccus. Environmental opportunistic pathogen,  mainly associated with UTIs especially in elderly patients with predisposing conditions. \nResistance has been reported sulfonamides and fluoroquinolones.\n','Amoxicillin.\nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nNitrofurantoin.\nFosfomycin.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nVancomycin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem. \n\n\n\n',1,'NULL','','Amoxicillin.\nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nNitrofurantoin.\nFosfomycin.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nVancomycin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem. \n\n\n\n','Amoxicillin.\nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nNitrofurantoin.\nFosfomycin.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nVancomycin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem. \n\n\n\n','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','Amoxicillin.\nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nNitrofurantoin.\nFosfomycin.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nVancomycin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem.','Amoxicillin.\nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nNitrofurantoin.\nFosfomycin.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nVancomycin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem.','Amoxicillin.\nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nNitrofurantoin.\nFosfomycin.\nVancomycin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem.','Amoxicillin.\nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nNitrofurantoin.\nFosfomycin.\nVancomycin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem.','Amoxicillin.\nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nNitrofurantoin.\nFosfomycin.\nVancomycin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem.','','','','','','','','','','','','','',''),
(21,'Alloscardovia Omnicolens','Anaerobic Gram-positive rod, related to Bifidbacteremium. Present in normal gut flora; a rare pathogen, often in mixed infection.\nPossible resistance to macrolides and fluoroquinolones.\nLimited effectiveness of metronidazole, nitrofurantoin, fosfomycin, and gentamicin have been reported.\nPLEASE NOTE: Pathogenicity unclear, may be a contaminant. Treat if symptomatic. If more pathogenic bacteria are present, treatment choices should prioritize them. \n','Penicillin.\nAmpicillin, Amoxicillin.\nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nTigecycline. \nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem. \n\n\n\n\n',1,'NULL','0','Penicillin.\nAmpicillin, Amoxicillin.\nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem. \n\n\n\n\n','Penicillin.\nAmpicillin, Amoxicillin.\nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem. \n\n\n\n\n','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','Penicillin.\nAmpicillin, Amoxicillin.\nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nTigecycline. \nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem.','Penicillin.\nAmpicillin, Amoxicillin.\nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nTigecycline. \nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem.','Penicillin.\nAmpicillin, Amoxicillin.\nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nTigecycline. \nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem.','Penicillin.\nAmpicillin, Amoxicillin.\nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem. \n\n\n\n\n','Penicillin.\nAmpicillin, Amoxicillin.\nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem. \n\n\n\n\n','','','','','','','','','','','',''),
(22,'Corynebacterium riegelii','Facultative anaerobic Gram-positive rod. Commensal species; it’s a common contaminant, rarely pathogenic.\nMay cause opportunistic infections in compromised patients.Resistant to fosfomycin. \nMulti-drug resistance can occur.\nPLEASE NOTE: Pathogenicity unclear, may be a contaminant. Treat if symptomatic. If more pathogenic bacteria are present, treatment choices should prioritize them. \n','Penicillin.\nVancomycin.\nGentamicin.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \n',1,'NULL','0','Penicillin.\nVancomycin.\nGentamicin.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \n','Penicillin.\nVancomycin.\nGentamicin.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \n','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','Penicillin.\nVancomycin.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \n','Penicillin.\nVancomycin.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \n','','','','','','','','','','','',''),
(23,'Enterococcus faecalis','Facultative anaerobic, gram-positive bacteria. Component of normal colonic flora and ubiquitous in the environment. A common cause of uncomplicated, complicated and recurrent UTIs, often catheter or instrumentation-associated.\nIntrinsic resistance to TMP-SMX and Aminoglycosides.\nPossible resistance to Macrolides.\nPlasmid-mediated resistance to Vancomycin (vanA, VanB) common.\nPlease note: Fluoroquinolone resistance may occur without the expression of the regular Qnr markers) due to chromosomal mutations and other mechanisms.\nPlease Note: Infectious disease consultation is recommended for complicated Vancomycin-resistant infections.\n','Penicillin G.\nAmpicillin, Amoxicillin.\nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nNitrofurantoin.\nFosfomycin.\nLevofloxacin.\nVancomycin.\nDaptomycin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.\n',1,'NULL','','Penicillin G.\nAmpicillin, Amoxicillin.\nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nNitrofurantoin.\nFosfomycin.\nLevofloxacin.\nVancomycin.\nDaptomycin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.\n','Penicillin G.\nAmpicillin, Amoxicillin.\nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nNitrofurantoin.\nFosfomycin.\nLevofloxacin.\nVancomycin.\nDaptomycin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.\n','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','Penicillin G.\nAmpicillin, Amoxicillin.\nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nNitrofurantoin.\nFosfomycin.\nVancomycin.\nDaptomycin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.\n\n','Penicillin G.\nAmpicillin, Amoxicillin.\nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nNitrofurantoin.\nFosfomycin.\nVancomycin.\nDaptomycin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.\n\n','Penicillin G.\nAmpicillin, Amoxicillin.\nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nNitrofurantoin.\nFosfomycin.\nVancomycin.\nDaptomycin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.\n\n','','','','','Linezolid.\nAmpicillin, Amoxicillin.\nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nNitrofurantoin.\nFosfomycin.\