(25,'Staphylococcus aureus','Aerobic, gram-positive cocci. A rare cause of UTIs, except in patients with risk factors for urinary tract colonization. Causes complicated and recurrent UTIs.\nMost isolates are penicillin-resistant.\nmecA marker (MRSA) leads to resistance to methicillin,  oxacillin,  nafcillin, and cephalosporins.\nPlease note: Fluoroquinolone resistance may occur without the regular Qnr markers, due to chromosomal mutations and other mechanisms.\nVancomycin resistance (vanA marker) may occur with long-term use.\nMacrolides resistance is possible due to erm genes.\n','TMP-SMX.\nNitrofurantoin.\nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nCephalexin.\nCefazolin.\nLevofloxacin.\nDaptomycin.\nClindamycin.\nVancomycin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.',1,'NULL','','TMP-SMX.\nNitrofurantoin.\nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nCephalexin.\nCefazolin.\nLevofloxacin.\nDaptomycin.\nClindamycin.\nVancomycin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.','TMP-SMX.\nNitrofurantoin.\nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nCephalexin.\nCefazolin.\nLevofloxacin.\nDaptomycin.\nClindamycin.\nVancomycin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','TMP-SMX.\nNitrofurantoin.\nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nCephalexin.\nCefazolin.\nDaptomycin.\nClindamycin.\nVancomycin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem, Ertapenem.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.','TMP-SMX.\nNitrofurantoin.\nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nCephalexin.\nCefazolin.\nDaptomycin.\nClindamycin.\nVancomycin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem, Ertapenem.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.','TMP-SMX.\nNitrofurantoin.\nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nCephalexin.\nCefazolin.\nDaptomycin.\nClindamycin.\nVancomycin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem, Ertapenem.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.'