(27,'Staphylococcus epidermidis','Aerobic, gram-positive cocci. Predominantly found on skin and mucous membranes. Almost always either a contaminant or a nosocomial pathogen. Important cause of prosthetic or implantable device infections, vascular catheters, peritoneal dialysis catheters. Strains are often methicillin-resistant.\nmecA, femA markers (MRSA) lead to resistance to methicillin, oxacillin, nafcillin, and cephalosporins.\n','Vancomycin, Daptomycin.\nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nTMP-SMX.\nCephalexin, Cefdinir.\nLevofloxacin.\nCefazolin, Cefepime.\nLinezolid.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.\n\n\n',1,'NULL','','Vancomycin, Daptomycin.\nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nTMP-SMX.\nCephalexin, Cefdinir.\nLevofloxacin.\nCefazolin, Cefepime.\nLinezolid.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.\n\n\n','Vancomycin, Daptomycin.\nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nTMP-SMX.\nCephalexin, Cefdinir.\nLevofloxacin.\nCefazolin, Cefepime.\nLinezolid.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.\n\n\n','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','Nitrofurantoin.\nDaptomycin.\nNafcillin, Oxacillin, Cefazolin. \nRifampin + TMP-SMX.\nLinezolid.','Nitrofurantoin.\nDaptomycin.\nNafcillin, Oxacillin, Cefazolin. \nRifampin + TMP-SMX.\nLinezolid.','Nitrofurantoin.\nDaptomycin.\nNafcillin, Oxacillin, Cefazolin. \nRifampin + TMP-SMX.\nLinezolid.','','','Ceftaroline.\nVancomycin. Daptomycin. \nLinezolid.','Ceftaroline.\nVancomycin. Daptomycin. \nLinezolid.','','','','','Vancomycin, Daptomycin.\nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nTMP-SMX.\nCephalexin, Cefdinir.\nLevofloxacin.\nCefazolin, Cefepime.\nLinezolid.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.\n','Vancomycin, Daptomycin.\nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nTMP-SMX.\nCephalexin, Cefdinir.\nLevofloxacin.\nCefazolin, Cefepime.\nLinezolid.\nImipenem-C