(29,'Staphylococcus saprophyticus','Aerobic, gram-positive cocci. Part of the normal GU tract flora. 2nd most common cause of uncomplicated UTIs, especially in young sexually active females. It may also cause complicated and recurrent UTIs.\nmecA, femA markers are common (MRSA), leading to resistance to methicillin, oxacillin, nafcillin, and cephalosporins.\nVancomycin resistance (vanA marker) may occur with long-term use.\nMacrolides resistance is possible due to erm genes.\nPlease note: Fluoroquinolone resistance may occur without the regular Qnr markers, due to chromosomal mutations and other mechanisms.','Amoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nNitrofurantoin.\nTMP-SMX.\nCephalexin.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nCefazolin, Cefepime, Ceftaroline.\nClindamycin.\nVancomycin, Daptomycin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem, Ertapenem.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.\n\n',1,'NULL','','Amoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nNitrofurantoin.\nTMP-SMX.\nCephalexin.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nCefazolin, Cefepime, Ceftaroline.\nClindamycin.\nVancomycin, Daptomycin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem, Ertapenem.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.\n\n','Amoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nNitrofurantoin.\nTMP-SMX.\nCephalexin.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nCefazolin, Cefepime, Ceftaroline.\nClindamycin.\nVancomycin, Daptomycin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem, Ertapenem.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.\n\n','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','Amoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nNitrofurantoin.\nTMP-SMX.\nCephalexin.\nCefazolin, Cefepime, Ceftaroline.\nClindamycin.\nVancomycin, Daptomycin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem, Ertapenem.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.','Amoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nNitrofurantoin.\nTMP-SMX.\nCephalexin.\nCefazolin, Cefepime, Ceftaroline.\nClindamycin.\nVancomycin, Daptomycin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem, Ertapenem.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.','Amoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nNitrofurantoin.\nTMP-SMX.\nCephalexin.\nCefazolin, Cefepime, Ceftaroline.\nClindamycin.\nVancomycin, Daptomycin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem, Ertapenem.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.','','','Nitrofurantoin.\nTMP-SMX.\nClindamycin.\nVancomycin, Daptomycin.\nCeftaroline.\n\n','Nitrofurantoin.\nTMP-SMX.\nClindamycin.\nVancomycin, Daptomycin.\nCeftaroline.\n\n','Amoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nNitrofurantoin.\nTMP-SMX.\nClindamycin.\nDaptomycin.\n','Amoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nNitrofurantoin.\nTMP-SMX.\nClindamycin.\nDaptomycin.\n','Amoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nNitrofurantoin.\nTMP-SMX.\nClindamycin.\nDaptomycin.\n','Amoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nNitrofurantoin.\nTMP-SMX.\nClindamycin.\nDaptomycin.\n','Amoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nNitrofurantoin.\nTMP-SMX.\nCephalexin.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nCefazolin, Cefepime, Ceftaroline.\nVancomycin, Daptomycin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem, Ertapenem.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.','Amoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nNitrofurantoin.\nTMP-SMX.\nCephalexin.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nCefazolin, Cefepime, Ceftaroline.\nVancomycin, Daptomycin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem, Ertapenem.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.','Amoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nNitrofurantoin.\nTMP-SMX.\nCephalexin.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nCefazolin, Cefepime, Ceftaroline.\nVancomycin, Daptomycin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem, Ertapenem.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.','Amoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nNitrofurantoin.\nTMP-SMX.\nCephalexin.\nCiprofloxacin, Levofloxacin. \nCefazolin, Cefepime, Ceftaroline.\nVancomycin, Daptomycin.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem, Ertapenem.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.','',''),
(30,'Streptococcus agalactiae','Gram-positive, Group B streptococcus. Normal commensal of the GU tract; recovered from about 10 percent of urine samples. Causes less than 5% of UTIs (asymptomatic bacteriuria, cystitis, pyelonephritis). More susceptible are neonates, pregnant women, the elderly, and the immunocompromised.\nResistance is common to Macrolides, methicillin, and cephalosporins.\nPlease note: Fluoroquinolone resistance may occur without the Qnr markers due to chromosomal mutations and other mechanisms.\nVancomycin resistance is uncommon but possible.','Penicillin G. \nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nCephalexin.\nLevofloxacin.\nCefazolin, Cefepime, Ceftaroline.\nVancomycin, Daptomycin.\nLinezolid.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.',1,'NULL','','Penicillin G. \nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nCephalexin.\nLevofloxacin.\nCefazolin, Cefepime, Ceftaroline.\nVancomycin, Daptomycin.\nLinezolid.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.','Penicillin G. \nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nCephalexin.\nLevofloxacin.\nCefazolin, Cefepime, Ceftaroline.\nVancomycin, Daptomycin.\nLinezolid.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','','Penicillin G. \nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nCephalexin.\nCefazolin, Cefepime, Ceftaroline.\nVancomycin, Daptomycin.\nLinezolid.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem, Ertapenem.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.','Penicillin G. \nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nCephalexin.\nCefazolin, Cefepime, Ceftaroline.\nVancomycin, Daptomycin.\nLinezolid.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem, Ertapenem.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam.\nImipenem-Cilastatin-Relebactam.','Penicillin G. \nAmoxicillin-Clavulanate.\nCephalexin.\nCefazolin, Cefepime, Ceftaroline.\nVancomycin, Daptomycin.\nLinezolid.\nImipenem-Cilastatin, Meropenem, Ertapenem.\nMeropenem-Vaborbactam