(488,'METHAMPHETAMINE','METHAMPHETAMINE < Cutoff','METHAMPHETAMINE','3-5 days','48 hours','Cutoff','ILLICIT - Methamphetamine is identified with two isomers D Methamphetamine  (RX and ILLICIT ,Most common) and L Methamphetamine( Nasal inhaler over the counter) its detection may arise from methamphetamine-containing drugs( Desoxyn) Illicit (Crystal meth) or metabolism of  selegiline, which is metabolized to both methamphetamine and  amphetamine. Methamphetamine is metabolized to amphetamine. L Methamphetamine is currently known to be available in OTC nasal inhalers and will present as Methamphetamine in this test. Methamphetamine D/L isomer test needed to differentiate the two.',NULL),
