(9,'pcr',0,19,'<div style=\"font-size:9px;padding-top:7px\">Disclaimer: This test was developed, and its performance characteristics determined by New Lab Laboratory. It has not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration. The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary. This test is used for clinical purpose. It should not be regarded as investigational or for research. This laboratory is certified under the Clinical Laboratory Improvement Amendments of 1988 (CLIA-88) as qualified to perform high complexity clinical laboratory testing. This panel does not distinguish between commensal and pathogenic bacterium. Detection of pathogens must be evaluated in consideration of clinical symptoms as well as the timeframe of which has elapsed between the time of high symptomatic response and specimen collection for proper diagnosis by a licensed medical professional. For patients experiencing a bacterium, parasitic or viral infection that is not denoted as a target within the panel, the infection cause will not be detected.</div>','0000-00-00','0000-00-00','2022-06-07 21:20:52',1,''),
(10,'pcr',0,8,'<br><i>Disclaimer: This test was developed, and its performance characteristics determined by New Lab Laboratory. It has not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration. The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary. This test is used for clinical purpose. It should not be regarded as investigational or for research. This laboratory is certified under the Clinical Laboratory Improvement Amendments of 1988 (CLIA-88) as qualified to perform high complexity clinical laboratory testing. This panel does not distinguish between commensal and pathogenic bacterium. Detection of pathogens must be evaluated in consideration of clinical symptoms as well as the timeframe of which has elapsed between the time of high symptomatic response and specimen collection for proper diagnosis by a licensed medical professional. For patients experiencing a bacterium, parasitic or viral infection that is not denoted as a target within the panel, the infection cause will not be detected. Enterobacter aerogenes tested within this panel is also accepted by the nomenclature of Klebsiella aerogenes.</i>','2022-12-05','0000-00-00','2022-12-08 13:56:55',1,''),
